<title>BELGIUM: EU clears Swedish CO2 fiscal measures.</title>
<headline>EU clears Swedish CO2 fiscal measures.</headline>
<text>
<p>BRUSSELS, Dec 4 (Reuter) The European Commission said on Wednesday it had approved a Swedish plan to offer certain companies relief from taxes on carbon dioxide (CO2) use.</p>
<p>The Swedish plan will increase the CO2 tax paid by the manufacturing industry from 25 percent of what other sectors pay to 50 percent. But high energy-consuming firms will benefit from tax relief, which the Commission said could be considered state aid.</p>
<p>The Commission said it cleared the plan because its environmental objectives were in line with EU objectives and that the competitiveness of the concerned sectors would be put at risk without relief. It noted that the scheme was due to expire at the end of 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;These prerequisites meet the conditions stipulated by the guidelines applicable to state aid for environmental protection,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6800</p>
